  "review_notes": [
    "Ποντικόν is a single adjective rendered 'a man of Pontus'; the head sits on 'Pontus' per rule 66, 'man' being the generic completion. Heading on 'man' is not defensible here since it glosses nothing.",
    "καί before Priscilla is aligned to 'with', the word the ASV wrote for the connective; leaving it unrepresented and giving 'with' to the accusative was the competing reading and is weaker, since no preposition is expressed."
